    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="7">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 7</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="312" ed="#liebermann"/>Licceteras<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_7.lnote.oe.15"/> ⁊ leogeras, ryperas ⁊ reaferas Godes graman habban, butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_7.lnote.oe.2"/> hig geswican<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_7.lnote.oe.16"/> ⁊ þe deoppar gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="312" ed="#liebermann"/>Liceteras ⁊ leogeras, ryperas ⁊ hreaferas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_7.lnote.oe.5"/> Godes graman habban, buton hig geswican ⁊ ðe deoppor gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="312" ed="#liebermann"/>Licceras<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_7.lnote.oe.5-2"/> ⁊ leogeras, reperas ⁊ reaferas Godes graman habban, buton hig geswycan ⁊ þe deoppor gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-d-frags"><pb n="312" ed="#liebermann"/>[⁊] Liceteras ⁊ leogeras, riperas ⁊ reaferas Godes graman habban, buton hig geswican.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="313" ed="#liebermann"/>Liguritores<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#IICn_7.lnote.oe.18"/> (seductores<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#IICn_7.lnote.oe.19"/>; adulatores<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#IICn_7.lnote.oe.20"/>), mendaces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_7.lnote.oe.21"/>, rapaces raptores Dei grauamen habeant, nisi cessent et prolixius emendent.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="313" ed="#liebermann"/>Adulatores, mendaces, pauperum spoliatores et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IICn_7.lnote.oe.9"/> raptores cito iram Dei incurrant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_7.lnote.oe.10"/>, nisi resipiscant et cessent et Deo satisfaciant.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_7.lnote.oe.11"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="7" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="313" ed="#liebermann"/>Parasiti, mentitores, raptores, dispoliatores Dei odio habeantur, nisi cessauerint et plene satisfecerint.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="7" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="178" ed="#robertson"/>Liceteras<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_7.robnote.fn.1"/> ⁊ leogeras, ryperas ⁊ hreaferas Godes graman habban, buton hig geswican ⁊ ðe deoppor gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="256" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Licceteras and leogeras, ryperas and reaferas Godes graman habban butan hig geswican and þe deoppar gebetan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="313" ed="#liebermann"/>Betrüger<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_7.lnote.de.1"/> (Lecker? <hi rend="italic">A</hi>) und Lügner, Räuber<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_7.lnote.de.2"/> und Plünderer sollen Gottes Zorn haben, ausser wenn sie [vom Bösen] abstehen und um so tiefer büssen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Hypocrites (lickers? A) and liars, robbers and plunderers shall have God's anger, unless they desist [from evil] and atone all the more deeply.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IICn_7.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="179" ed="#robertson"/>Hypocrites and liars, robbers and plunderers shall incur the wrath of God, unless they desist and make amends to the utmost.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="463" ed="#whitelock"/>Hypocrites and liars, robbers and plunderers, shall incur God’s anger, unless they desist and atone very deeply.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="257" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Hypocrites and liars, thieves and looters will suffer God’s wrath unless they cease and most sincerely repent.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="313">Wulfstan 26. 114</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd.</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="93"><label>=</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-019">Cn 1018 10</ref> <quote>Cn 1018 10 = II Cn 7</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">A's ‘Licceras’ was the reading before Quadr. and Consiliatio.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 313, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">312</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">313</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ligurr. <hi rend="italic">THk; fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ligurr. THk; lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">313</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr. Dm;</hi> id est se. <hi rend="italic">T; fehlt KRHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above Dm; id est se. T; lacking in KRHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">313</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> ad. <hi rend="italic">R; fehlt übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only ad. R; lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">313</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">doppelt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">twice K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">312</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Licceras ⁊ leogoras, rep. ⁊ reafaras <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Licceras ⁊ leogoras, rep. ⁊ reafaras Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">312</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">buton <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">buton Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">312</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">geswycan ⁊ ðe deopor <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">geswycan ⁊ ðe deopor Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.oe.5-2" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">312</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">diese Verlesung lag Quadr. und Consil. vor</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Quadr. and Consil. had this misreading before them</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">313</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et r. <hi rend="italic">am Rande Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et r. in the margin Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">313</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rent <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rent Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">313</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">7, 1 <hi rend="italic">fehlt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">7, 1 lacking</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">203</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Licetere, hypocrita vel fictor</hi> glossierend, heisst u. a. der Weisheit heuchelnde Teufel; <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 52; ‘false in deed and word’ übersetzt Toller; <hi rend="italic">adulator</hi> ist zu eng; <hi rend="italic">parasita</hi> und <hi rend="italic">ligurritor</hi> (dieses auch durch Gleichklang suggeriert) übersetzen wohl A's <hi rend="italic">liccere</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Licetere</hi>, glossing <hi rend="italic">hypocrita vel fictor</hi>, is used, among others, of the devil feigning wisdom; <hi rend="italic">Hom. n</hi>. Wulfstan 52; Toller translates ‘false in deed and word’; <hi rend="italic">adulator</hi> is too narrow; <hi rend="italic">parasita</hi> and <hi rend="italic">ligurritor</hi> (the latter also suggested by similarity of sound) probably translate A’s <hi rend="italic">liccere</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_7.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">203</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">rypere</hi> und <hi rend="italic">reafere</hi>, auch <hi rend="italic">o</hi>. 4, 2¹ beisammen, sind in der Bed., nicht unterscheidbar; auch <hi rend="italic">woruldstruderas</hi> steht bisweilen daneben</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">rypere</hi> and <hi rend="italic">reafere</hi>, which also stand together <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 4, 2¹, cannot be distinguished in meaning; <hi rend="italic">woruldstruderas</hi> too sometimes stands alongside them</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IICn_7.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">352</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">The alliteration is again noteworthy.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_7.robnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">178</biblScope></bibl><label>Liceteras</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">licceras</hi> A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
